    "title": "Check for Understanding",
    "long_instructions": "##Human-Written and Computer-Learned Rules\r\nA photo app does three things:\r\n1. Puts screenshots in a Screenshots album.\r\n2. Groups photos of the same person together.\r\n3. Deletes photos in the trash after 30 days.\r\n\r\nWhich one is most likely a computer-learned rule? Explain how you know.",
    "teacher_markdown": "The answer is #2. A person can’t write exact steps that recognize every face, so the computer has to learn from many example photos. #1 and #3 are exact checks a person can write. A partial answer picks #2 but doesn’t explain why.",
